=== Generated Answer (model draft; check against evidence) ===
The paper explores three models for generating sentence vectors: averaging the vectors of the words in one sentence, paragraph vectors, and specific word vectors [3]. The first model, AVGWVEC, averages the vectors in the word sequence w = <w1, x2, ...wn>, using a word embedding matrix learned by the classical word2vec algorithm [3]. The second model, PARAVEC, trains paragraph vectors using the distributed memory model of paragraph vectors (PV-DM), an extension of word2vec in which the paragraph vectors are held in a matrix D and each paragraph is mapped to a unique vector [11]. The third model aims at improving classification results for a certain category—specifically, identifying the category BAS—by integrating cuewords into the embeddings [10]; in this case, BAS-specific word embeddings (BSWE) were trained, and then the same scheme of averaging the vectors in one sentence as in AVGWVEC was used [8].
